course: dictionary
lesson: 12350
title: Words that sound like their meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words copy the sound they describe. Say creaking slowly and you can almost hear a door groaning. When you meet a word like this, picture the sound or the action, and the meaning often becomes clear.
explain: «The creaking door opened slowly, and Amara froze.» The sound tells you the door is old or stiff, and it makes the story feel spooky. Ask yourself: what is happening, and how does it feel?
explain: Creaking can also describe something old that is struggling. «The creaking railway needs new trains.» Nothing in that sentence is making a sound. Look at the words around the word to know which meaning the writer means.
fact: Creaking means making a long, squeaky, groaning sound when wood, doors, floors or hinges move or bear weight.
fact: «Creak» is the verb. Its forms are creaks, creaked and creaking.
fact: «Creaking floorboards» means floorboards that make that groaning sound when someone walks on them.
fact: A creaking system or organisation is old and struggling to work well.
fact: In science, creaking comes from vibrations when things rub or bend, and vibrations are what we hear as sound.
exercise: «The creaking door opened slowly.» What is creaking? | A soft song sung by a child | *A long, squeaky groan from the door | A bright light shining through the gap | A loud bang like a firework
exercise: «The old stairs creaked under her feet.» Which word shows that the stairs made the sound? | stairs | feet | under | *creaked
exercise: «The creaking railway needs new trains.» What does creaking mean here? | *Old and struggling to work well | Full of happy passengers | Making a squeaky sound on purpose | Newly painted and shiny
test: «Floorboards creaked as the thief crept along the hall.» What does this tell the reader? | The floor is covered in soft carpet | The hall was freshly painted and quiet | *Someone may be nearby, and the story feels tense | The thief is a happy character
test: Hinges creak when they rub together. Which science idea does this show? | Plants need sunlight to grow | Light travels in straight lines | *Rubbing or bending makes vibrations that we hear as sound | Water boils at 100 degrees
exam: «The creaking floorboards warned Mia that someone was in the house.» What is the best meaning of creaking here? | A sweet smell from the kitchen | *A long, squeaky groan made by wood or floors | A pale, faded colour | A bright flash of light
